    "calculation": "First, calculate the number of unemployed in Croatia in 2015: 4887 * 0.421 * 0.074 = 152.25 The percentage of the workforce who are unemployed rose by 5% from 2010 to 2015, so the 2010 figure would be: 0.074 / 1.05 = 0.0705 or 7.048% The population of Croatia rose by 3.3% and so the population in 2010 would have been: 4887 / 1.033 = 4730.88 The number of unemployed in 2010 was: 4730.88 * 0.419 * 0.07048 = 139.708 The difference in numbers of people unemployed is then: 152.25 – 139.708 = 12.542 This is in thousands and so the answer is 12542.",
